From c91f29b0eb7446774521e190272af502a77374c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:55:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mce-amd-smca: avoid using a non-initialized bank type

As reported by Coverity:
 CID 1685827: (#1 of 1): Uninitialized scalar variable (UNINIT)
	12. uninit_use: Using uninitialized value bank_type.

the logic may end checking if bank_type >= N_SMCA_BANK_TYPES after
a loop that might not have initialized it.

Fix it by initializing the variable with N_SMCA_BANK_TYPES.

Signed-off-by: Mauro Carvalho Chehab <mchehab+huawei@kernel.org>
---
 events-arch-x86/mce-amd-smca.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/events-arch-x86/mce-amd-smca.c b/events-arch-x86/mce-amd-smca.c
index ac808c0..1041a3b 100644
--- a/events-arch-x86/mce-amd-smca.c
+++ b/events-arch-x86/mce-amd-smca.c
@@ -918,7 +918,7 @@ static inline void fixup_hwid(struct mce_priv *m, uint32_t *hwid_mcatype)
 /* Decode extended errors according to Scalable MCA specification */
 void decode_smca_error(struct mce_event *e, struct mce_priv *m)
 {
-	enum smca_bank_types bank_type;
+	enum smca_bank_types bank_type = N_SMCA_BANK_TYPES;
 	const char *ip_name;
 	uint32_t mcatype_hwid = 0;
 	unsigned short xec = (e->status >> 16) & 0x3f;
